{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch14wEajko4kRZeKf2Tz9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The neuron route is closed. The layer-4 anti-hard neurons are the model's general relevance units: they correlate with body overlap (0.45), title match (0.33) and answer presence (0.25). The \"pure distractor-promoter\" neurons contribute almost nothing (sum −0.017). Damping them would mainly weaken relevance as a whole, so it is not a targeted fix.\n\nThe length check is still in flight. Meanwhile I'll test whether layer-6 [CLS] has a length direction **orthogonal to the readout**: if so, the readout could be made to penalise length without being rescaled. I'll also see how it relates to the title-match direction.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: final [CLS] carries a paragraph-length direction distinct from the readout; it's the handle for a length-normalisation edit.\nX6c = cq(C[:, 6])\ndef cov_dir(X, f, use):  # covariance direction (statistic) of within-q centred X with feature f, on rows `use`\n    d = (X[use] * (f[use] - f[use].mean())[:, None]).mean(0); return d / np.linalg.norm(d)\nlenv = cov_dir(X6c, lnt, A); len_o = orth(lenv, [r_])\ntiv = cov_dir(X6c, tic, A & dist); ti_o = orth(tiv, [r_])\nprint(\"cos(len, r)=%.2f cos(title, r)=%.2f cos(len_o, ti_o)=%.2f\" % (lenv @ r_, tiv @ r_, len_o @ ti_o))\nfor nm, v in [(\"len_o\", len_o), (\"title_o\", ti_o)]:\n    p = X6c @ v\n    print(\"%-8s B: corr(log ntok)=%.2f corr(title)=%.2f corr(score)=%.2f corr(ov)=%.2f | B gold-sep=%.2f sd | within-q sd=%.3f (score-axis sd %.3f)\"\n          % (nm, np.corrcoef(p[~A], lnt[~A])[0,1], np.corrcoef(p[~A], tic[~A])[0,1], np.corrcoef(p[~A], s0c[~A])[0,1], np.corrcoef(p[~A], ovc[~A])[0,1],\n             (p[~A & gold].mean() - p[~A & dist].mean()) / p[~A].std(), p.std(), (X6c @ r_).std()))\n# statistic-only scan (A): adding -len_o or +title_o projection to the recorded score\nrows = []\nfor nm, v, sg in [(\"-len_o\", len_o, -1), (\"+title_o\", ti_o, 1)]:\n    p = C[:, 6] @ v; zz = (p - p.mean()) / cq(p).std()\n    for beta in [0.25, 0.5, 1.0]:\n        rows.append((nm, beta) + tuple(robust(FA, S0[A] + sg * beta * sdS * zz[A]).values()))\nprint(pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"dir\", \"beta\"] + list(robust(FA, S0[A]).keys())).to_string(index=False))\nnp.savez(WORK / \"dirs_len_title.npz\", len_o=len_o, ti_o=ti_o, r=r_)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4589,"cache_read_input_tokens":62297,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4589},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aabc22c4-c493-4939-8aac-1a1cdf219a55","uuid":"1537ac80-e590-4c1d-97f5-9c7123e25b0c","timestamp":"2026-11-13T14:16:23.272Z","request_id":"req_011Ch14wD3xXXkhVJv4hakrD"}
